WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.436
-My first guest tonight is one
of the biggest movie stars

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:04.937
on the planet!

00:00:04.937 --> 00:00:08.375
he produced and stars in
the new movie, "Jungle Cruise,"

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:11.544
Which is in theaters and on
Disney+, with premiere access

00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:15.281
July 30th, here is
Dwayne Johnson!

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:17.383
[ Cheers and applause ]
Oh, yeah!

00:00:17.383 --> 00:00:21.153
That's what I'm talking about!
Hey!

00:00:21.153 --> 00:00:23.122
Yes!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:23.122 --> 00:00:26.325
-Wow!
-That's what I'm talking about.

00:00:26.325 --> 00:00:28.928
-Wow!
-Yes!

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:30.096
[ Cheers and applause ]
Can you feel?

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:32.965
-Thank you.
-Can you feel the love?

00:00:32.965 --> 00:00:35.635
-I can feel the love
from that audience,

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:37.637
Thank you guys so much,
I love you back.

00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:40.507
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:40.507 --> 00:00:41.774
-We're so happy to see you.

00:00:41.774 --> 00:00:44.344
Thank you for
coming back, buddy.

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:45.978
We have a lot to talk about.

00:00:45.978 --> 00:00:49.516
I want to talk about, first,
you just finished filming

00:00:49.516 --> 00:00:52.718
"Black Atom" and here's some
photo of you,

00:00:52.718 --> 00:00:54.286
in the middle of filming,

00:00:54.286 --> 00:00:56.589
gosh you are ripped
in this thing.

00:00:56.589 --> 00:01:00.126
Like, that is unbelievable.
-Thank you.

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:01.995
-Now, no one trains harder
than you.

00:01:01.995 --> 00:01:03.296
No one trains harder
than you.

00:01:03.296 --> 00:01:06.299
I follow you on Instagram,
I see all these things

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:07.700
that you do, I go,
"Oh, my gosh."

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:08.934
And I remember that you've been
tyrannizing for this

00:01:08.934 --> 00:01:11.271
for two years, but you also do,
like, cheat meals

00:01:11.271 --> 00:01:13.806
every now and then,
when you're not training.

00:01:13.806 --> 00:01:16.409
What was your cheat meal for
this workout?

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:17.910
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:21.113
-Well, you know, I had been
training and preparing for

00:01:21.113 --> 00:01:24.517
"Black Atom" for a few years now
because I felt like it was,

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:29.088
you get one shot at creating,
hopefully creating something

00:01:29.088 --> 00:01:31.157
that's definitive in the world
of superheroes

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:33.159
and comic book lore
and mythology.

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:36.362
So, I really put in the work on
this one, Jimmy.

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:40.266
And, um, and as far as for the
cheat meals, I --

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:43.135
after that because that,
actually what you're seeing,

00:01:43.135 --> 00:01:46.606
was actually my very last day of
shooting "Black Atom"

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:48.974
So we wrapped
probably around midnight,

00:01:48.974 --> 00:01:54.380
and I would say by 1:30 a.m.,
I was face first in the biggest

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:57.650
pile of pancakes
you could imagine.

00:01:57.650 --> 00:02:00.052
[ Applause ]
-I know you love your pancakes.

00:02:00.052 --> 00:02:02.988
You also love your French toast,
I see every now and then.

00:02:02.988 --> 00:02:04.990
You're like French toast and,
was it peanut butter?

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:06.559
What do you put on there?

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:08.728
-Oh, dude, let me tell you,
now that you asked.

00:02:08.728 --> 00:02:11.064
I do big thick
brioche French toast.

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:13.732
I call it "Rock toast."
Four inches thick.

00:02:13.732 --> 00:02:16.402
Uh, we do peanut butter,
I'll do some butter,

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:19.606
I'll do some, uh,
teremana-infused syrup,

00:02:19.606 --> 00:02:21.808
I'll do coconut chips,
whipped cream,

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:25.912
and I bring new meaning to the
word "gluttony."

00:02:25.912 --> 00:02:28.681
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.681 --> 00:02:30.149
-How's the family, by the way?

00:02:30.149 --> 00:02:31.984
I know you just posted about
your daughter,

00:02:31.984 --> 00:02:34.654
your daughter's love --
she's probably three now, maybe?

00:02:34.654 --> 00:02:37.890
-Yes, Tia.
-Your daughter's love for

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:40.626
Aquaman -- she loves Aquaman.

00:02:40.626 --> 00:02:43.496
And there's a funny video of
you, because I know Jason Momoa

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:45.798
he was on our show and he sent a
nice video to wish her

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:47.933
happy birthday,
and, but here's a video

00:02:47.933 --> 00:02:49.835
to show you how much she love
Aquaman.

00:02:49.835 --> 00:02:51.504
Take a look at Tia
and Dwayne.

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:53.539
-Look what Aquaman did
to that man.

00:02:53.539 --> 00:02:57.410
-I saw what Aquaman just did.

00:02:57.410 --> 00:03:00.646
Who's cooler? Daddy?
-Aquaman.

00:03:00.646 --> 00:03:02.614
-Aquaman?
[ Audience moans ]

00:03:02.614 --> 00:03:06.218
[ Dwayne and Jimmy laugh ]
-Good timing. Good timing.

00:03:06.218 --> 00:03:08.821
It was great timing on her part
she didn't even let you say

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:11.591
Aqua-- like "Who's cooler,
Daddy?" "Aquaman."

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:14.227
She didn't even let you finish.
-Dude, she, she jumped

00:03:14.227 --> 00:03:16.696
right on that, which is great
for the ego,

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:21.801
but I gotta say that, you know,
in the world of celebrities,

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:24.637
you know, you never know
who's nice and who's kind

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:28.441
until you meet them or, or
really until, you know,

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:30.142
little children are involved.

00:03:30.142 --> 00:03:33.912
And I've known Jason for a very
long time now.

00:03:33.912 --> 00:03:36.415
I'm very proud of his career
and all the things

00:03:36.415 --> 00:03:38.184
that's he's been doing.

00:03:38.184 --> 00:03:41.854
So, I gotta tell you, I called
up Jason, I said,

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:44.857
"Man, I know you're busy,
you're on set,

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:48.294
but my daughter, specifically my
three-year-old daughter,

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:50.796
she adores you, we watch
'Aquaman' all the time.

00:03:50.796 --> 00:03:53.632
She thinks you're way cooler
than Daddy.

00:03:53.632 --> 00:03:55.200
And it's her birthday
coming up, man."

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:59.305
And he sent the most beautiful
birthday video to Tia,

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:02.407
as well as to Jazzy.

00:04:02.407 --> 00:04:05.210
Aquaman invited them to Hawaii
where we're gonna swim

00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:07.479
in the ocean together and we're
gonna go rock climbing.

00:04:07.479 --> 00:04:09.848
He made all these promises that
make me look bad, Jimmy.

00:04:09.848 --> 00:04:12.284
-Yeah, of course.
Exactly.

00:04:12.284 --> 00:04:14.454
You know what, I want to ask,
more importantly,

00:04:14.454 --> 00:04:17.089
for me, you know my relationship
with your mom.

00:04:17.089 --> 00:04:20.693
How is your mom doing? Because
last time she was on the show,

00:04:20.693 --> 00:04:22.595
I don't know if you guys saw
this but...

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:24.363
-[ Laughs ]
-...she happened to be around.

00:04:24.363 --> 00:04:26.466
I was talking about your mom and
playing ukulele.

00:04:26.466 --> 00:04:28.601
And you're like, "She's actually
here, if you want to see her."

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:32.071
She came in, totally hijacked
the interview

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:35.441
and played beautiful
ukulele music.

00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:41.013
And how is she doing? Did fame
go to her head? Is she, uh?

00:04:41.013 --> 00:04:44.416
-I don't know. I can't talk to
her, she's a diva now.

00:04:44.416 --> 00:04:47.086
-[ Laughs ]
-I have to go through her

00:04:47.086 --> 00:04:49.922
assistant's assistant assistant
to talk to my mom.

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:51.657
But it was crazy,
I remember that.

00:04:51.657 --> 00:04:53.859
Well, first of all,
she loves you.

00:04:53.859 --> 00:04:57.330
She adores you and she thinks
you're the greatest thing

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:59.031
walking God's green earth,
Jimmy.

00:04:59.031 --> 00:05:01.267
So, when she pulled out that
ukulele I --

00:05:01.267 --> 00:05:03.703
both you and I had no idea where
she was gonna go.

00:05:03.703 --> 00:05:05.304
-So scared.
-And she starts singing

00:05:05.304 --> 00:05:07.407
♪ We love you, Jimmy ♪
-Yes!

00:05:07.407 --> 00:05:09.842
-♪ Oh, yes, it's true ♪
I was like, wait, mom, what?

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:12.511
-[ Laughs ] It was, those
moments you can't plan.

00:05:12.511 --> 00:05:14.881
Please give her my love,
please, buddy.

00:05:14.881 --> 00:05:18.083
-I will.
-I want to talk about teremana.

00:05:18.083 --> 00:05:20.919
Your tequila. This is --
it's the fastest-growing

00:05:20.919 --> 00:05:23.389
spirits brand to date.

00:05:23.389 --> 00:05:25.924
The fastest-growing spirits
of any, to date.

00:05:25.924 --> 00:05:30.496
[ Cheers and applause ]
Not too shabby, buddy.

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:33.099
-Yes, thank you very much.
-There's a thing called

00:05:33.099 --> 00:05:36.802
the Mana Mobile and if it
doesn't stop by my house

00:05:36.802 --> 00:05:37.970
where can I see it?

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:41.007
Where can I see this thing
and what is this?

00:05:41.007 --> 00:05:44.843
-Dude that -- so the Mana Mobile
serves tacos,

00:05:44.843 --> 00:05:49.515
it serves special recipes,
it serves teremana cocktails,

00:05:49.515 --> 00:05:52.050
it serves french toast.

00:05:52.050 --> 00:05:55.021
And that Mana Mobile is going
coast to coast.

00:05:55.021 --> 00:05:57.389
Multiple Mana Mobiles are going
coast to coast.

00:05:57.389 --> 00:06:00.125
And we wanted to bring
the mana to the people.

00:06:00.125 --> 00:06:03.328
So that Mana Mobile will be
going to fire stations,

00:06:03.328 --> 00:06:08.534
military bases,
college campuses, communities,

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:11.671
food festivals, you name it, the
Mana Mobile is coming to you.

00:06:11.671 --> 00:06:13.373
-Yeah, look out
for the Mana Mobile.

